    </node>
    <node id="载荷">
      <data key="d0">载荷</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Load refers to the force applied to a mechanical component during operation.&lt;SEP&gt;载荷是指作用在机械设备上的外力。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4d0a9d9911a119de81d8e1c006a65b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512a577252da2b6701f9a8656b72a4ab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752706</data>
    </node>
    <node id="磨损">
      <data key="d0">磨损</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Wear, or磨损 in Chinese, refers to the process of material loss from a part due to use, which necessitates repair. It is a common failure mode in mechanical components and can lead to the failure of mechanical equipment. This phenomenon involves the gradual removal of material from the surface of an object, primarily caused by friction and other actions, including surface contact or friction. It is characterized by the gradual destruction of materials due to these factors, and can be attributed to various causes such as friction, impact, and relative motion between parts. Specifically, wear in mechanical components is the result of surface damage caused by the friction and wear that occurs during the operational life of the equipment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89c33b1709aba69300fa32c8a1899f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512a577252da2b6701f9a8656b72a4ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec89303a6088293925f758d2cbbf49ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51df47410675f88b40ee5775ddf467a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2714adef57ebf31098afe9ba8240006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1971066a581f0990af3c8c34cc992fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9aa1cf69ef2f507f89adeb826f8b153</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752708</data>
    </node>
    <node id="疲劳破坏">
      <data key="d0">疲劳破坏</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">疲劳破坏是指零件在交变载荷作用下，因反复应力而导致的失效。</data>
