      <data key="d3">chunk-1d3b4640c2971d1da053004b90733694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="焊接或打磨容器或管道">
      <data key="d0">焊接或打磨容器或管道</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Welding or grinding containers or pipes containing flammable, explosive, or toxic substances requires careful handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d3b4640c2971d1da053004b90733694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="孔口">
      <data key="d0">孔口</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Holes or openings in equipment that need to be opened for maintenance or repair.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d3b4640c2971d1da053004b90733694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="废油、废面纱">
      <data key="d0">废油、废面纱</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Waste oil and waste wadding should be disposed of properly and not littered on the ground.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d3b4640c2971d1da053004b90733694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="原材料、半成品、成品堆放">
      <data key="d0">原材料、半成品、成品堆放</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Raw materials, semi-finished products, and finished goods should be neatly stacked to prevent blockages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d3b4640c2971d1da053004b90733694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="润滑及液压系统清洁">
      <data key="d0">润滑及液压系统清洁</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cleaning the lubrication and hydraulic systems of equipment is essential for proper operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d3b4640c2971d1da053004b90733694</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="频谱分析">
      <data key="d0">频谱分析</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of performing frequency spectrum analysis is a method used in equipment diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障诊断过程">
      <data key="d0">故障诊断过程</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The fault diagnosis process is a cyclic process that involves multiple iterations of diagnostic cycles to gradually deepen understanding and improve accuracy in identifying the root cause of a complex fault.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="简易诊断技术">
      <data key="d0">简易诊断技术</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Simplified diagnostic technology is a method of quickly assessing the technical state of equipment using simple instruments and methods, generally including the use of diagnostic instruments and detection meters, and the involvement of maintenance personnel in the production site for analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="精密诊断技术">
      <data key="d0">精密诊断技术</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Precise diagnostic technology is a method of making detailed evaluations of equipment that cannot be diagnosed by simplified diagnostic technology, generally involving the use of complex diagnostic analysis instruments and the involvement of experienced engineers and experts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障发生规律">
      <data key="d0">故障发生规律</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The characteristics of equipment failure include an increased likelihood of failure with the increase in equipment use years and the randomness of failure occurrence, making it difficult to predict the exact time of occurrence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障率">
      <data key="d0">故障率</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fault rate is the conditional probability of a failure occurring in a time interval dt after t, which is represented by λ(t).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障率浴盆曲线">
      <data key="d0">故障率浴盆曲线</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The fault rate bathtub curve illustrates the three stages of equipment failure rates: early failure period, random failure period, and wear-out failure period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="早期故障期">
      <data key="d0">早期故障期</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The early failure period is characterized by a high failure rate, which rapidly decreases with the increase in equipment working time. Early failures are generally caused by design or manufacturing defects.&lt;SEP&gt;The early failure phase is a period characterized by a high failure rate that rapidly decreases with the increase of equipment operating time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="随机故障期">
      <data key="d0">随机故障期</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The random failure period is a stage where the failure rate remains relatively constant, and it is difficult to predict the exact time of failure.&lt;SEP&gt;The random failure phase is a period with a low and stable failure rate, resembling a constant value.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="耗损故障期">
      <data key="d0">耗损故障期</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The wear-out failure period is the stage where the failure rate increases with the increase in equipment working time due to aging and wear.&lt;SEP&gt;The wear-out failure phase is characterized by an increasing failure rate with the increase of operating time, indicating that the equipment is approaching major maintenance or the end of its life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="设备特征参数">
      <data key="d0">设备特征参数</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Equipment feature parameters are the specific attributes used to assess the condition of equipment during diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="允许参数">
      <data key="d0">允许参数</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Allowable parameters are the standards used to determine if equipment is within an acceptable range for operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="判别参数">
      <data key="d0">判别参数</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminant parameters are used to differentiate between normal and abnormal equipment conditions during diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="判别准则">
      <data key="d0">判别准则</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Discriminant criteria are the rules established to evaluate and determine the state of equipment during fault diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="诊断策略">
      <data key="d0">诊断策略</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Diagnostic strategies are the methods and approaches used to diagnose equipment faults effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="对策和措施">
      <data key="d0">对策和措施</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Countermeasures and measures are the actions taken to address equipment issues based on the diagnosis results.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="信号预测">
      <data key="d0">信号预测</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Signal prediction involves forecasting the potential future state of equipment based on current signal analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="趋势分析">
      <data key="d0">趋势分析</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Trend analysis is a method used to predict the future behavior of equipment based on current trends.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="循环诊断">
      <data key="d0">循环诊断</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Cyclic diagnosis refers to the iterative process of diagnosing equipment faults to deepen understanding and improve accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="设备维护检修人员">
      <data key="d0">设备维护检修人员</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Equipment maintenance and repair personnel are the individuals responsible for diagnosing and fixing equipment issues in the production site.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="生产现场">
      <data key="d0">生产现场</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The production site is the location where equipment is operated and maintained.&lt;SEP&gt;生产现场是指液压系统实际运行和操作的地方。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5313a1b2bfcb93c2968ea3919437605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障信号">
      <data key="d0">故障信号</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fault signals are the indicators that something is wrong with the equipment, often captured during diagnostic processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="存储建档">
      <data key="d0">存储建档</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Storage and documentation involve recording and archiving fault signals for future reference and analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="设备状态监测">
      <data key="d0">设备状态监测</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Equipment state monitoring is the process of regularly or continuously monitoring the technical state of equipment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="警报或自动停机">
      <data key="d0">警报或自动停机</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Alarms or automatic shutdown are safety features that activate when equipment is operating outside of safe parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="安装调试阶段">
      <data key="d0">安装调试阶段</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The installation and debugging stage is the initial phase of equipment setup where potential issues are identified and resolved.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="维护阶段">
      <data key="d0">维护阶段</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The maintenance stage is the ongoing process of ensuring the proper functioning of equipment over its lifespan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="事故隐患">
      <data key="d0">事故隐患</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Accident隐患refers to potential dangers or risks that could lead to equipment failure or accidents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="设备的劣化趋势">
      <data key="d0">设备的劣化趋势</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The deterioration trend of equipment refers to the progressive decline in the performance or condition of equipment over time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="复杂诊断分析仪器">
      <data key="d0">复杂诊断分析仪器</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Complex diagnostic analysis instruments are advanced tools used for detailed equipment diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="诊断中心">
      <data key="d0">诊断中心</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The diagnostic center is a facility where equipment diagnostics are performed by trained professionals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障产生部位">
      <data key="d0">故障产生部位</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fault location refers to the specific part of the equipment where the failure has occurred.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障原因">
      <data key="d0">故障原因</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fault cause refers to the underlying reason why a failure has occurred in the equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;The causes of a fault in a system or component.&lt;SEP&gt;The reasons for crawling failure include factors like improper assembly, reactive forces, and worn-out components or oil contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;The underlying cause of a malfunction or problem in a system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-205e5b50ed08e4587699576c3110fefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e927ef66eacdc3741d7a8dbda2d77531&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45c7f498930072d1430aac19bea884b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="故障类型">
      <data key="d0">故障类型</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fault type refers to the classification of the failure based on its characteristics and effects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="维修决策">
      <data key="d0">维修决策</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Maintenance decisions are the actions taken based on the diagnosis of equipment faults to facilitate repairs.&lt;SEP&gt;维修决策是指根据设备状况和维修需求做出的决策过程。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89c33b1709aba69300fa32c8a1899f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cde666ee942b8de11cef408152ad26cc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="磨损机理">
      <data key="d0">磨损机理</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Wear mechanism refers to the study of the causes and processes of wear in mechanical components, which is crucial for developing maintenance strategies and plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="磨合阶段">
      <data key="d0">磨合阶段</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The磨合阶段is the initial stage of component wear where the surface has microscopic peaks, resulting in a smaller actual contact area and high contact stress, leading to high plastic deformation and wear rate during operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="稳定磨损阶段">
      <data key="d0">稳定磨损阶段</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The stable wear stage is characterized by a low and stable wear rate, which is a long-lasting stage. However, towards the end, the wear rate increases relatively quickly, and the equipment can still operate for a while before reaching the critical wear point.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="急剧磨损阶段">
      <data key="d0">急剧磨损阶段</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The critical wear stage is marked by a significant change in friction conditions, leading to an abrupt increase in wear rate. This stage is associated with a significant decrease in mechanical efficiency and precision, and can potentially lead to equipment failure or accidents if not addressed promptly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="磨料磨损">
      <data key="d0">磨料磨损</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Abrasive wear occurs when a hard protrusion on one surface of a friction pair contacts another surface, or when hard particles such as dust or metallic particles in the air come into contact with both surfaces during relative motion, resulting in the transfer of material from one or both surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;磨料磨损是指金属表面由于磨料的作用而发生的磨损。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9784ee50339b8dae5e16fe13763d736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
    </node>
    <node id="疲劳磨损">
      <data key="d0">疲劳磨损</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fatigue wear is a form of wear where fatigue cracks occur on the surface of the friction pair under cyclic contact stress, resulting in the separation of tiny pieces or particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatigue wear is the formation of fatigue cracks in the surface of a friction pair under cyclic contact stress, leading to the separation of micro fragments or chips.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed1d66300ee50fa3b2a448b0a6e37ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752713</data>
