    <node id="黏着磨损">
      <data key="d0">黏着磨损</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of bearing failure caused by the sticking together of two sliding surfaces under pressure and heat.&lt;SEP&gt;Adhesive wear is a type of wear that occurs when two surfaces adhere to each other, causing material transfer from one surface to another.&lt;SEP&gt;Adhesive wear occurs when the material from one surface migrates to another surface due to 'cold welding' points during relative sliding.&lt;SEP&gt;黏着磨损是指金属表面由于材料粘附而发生的磨损。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9784ee50339b8dae5e16fe13763d736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed1d66300ee50fa3b2a448b0a6e37ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300b674808e0dab401bb885faad4bb34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
