      <data key="d0">微动磨损</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Micro-wear is a form of wear that occurs when two contacting objects undergo relative micro-amplitude vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Micro-wear is a type of wear that occurs due to the repeated motion of two surfaces in contact, leading to the gradual removal of material.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed1d66300ee50fa3b2a448b0a6e37ef8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f29046f6ed7b64daf3284ca274d836</data>
