    <node id="熔断器">
      <data key="d0">熔断器</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The '熔断器' (Fuse) is a critical protective device designed for low-voltage electrical systems. It serves to safeguard electrical circuits from the detrimental effects of overcurrents, preventing damage to equipment. These devices are widely employed in both industrial and general electrical applications. The primary function of a fuse is to disconnect the circuit automatically when it detects an overload or a short circuit, thereby preventing excessive current from flowing through the system. Fuses are characterized as safety devices that are typically removed and replaced individually to pinpoint the location of a fault within the circuit. In essence, the '熔断器' acts as a fusible cutout, disconnecting the circuit when the current exceeds a safe level, thereby ensuring the integrity and longevity of the electrical systems in which they are installed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee9c850f2bcdf0f748d9c6a77d4b1f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1971066a581f0990af3c8c34cc992fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9a307bb2e286ef8dcf8f76eb605627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efb58ef07953cfa7d2761587f8cf0115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1e8bd51981f8100b6363185c3e9517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e809e2424701c731a2da5e003621fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da71d339cddfe10d4c69101282de0424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7717f9c647b8d45b1cefa44db848f23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcf0dd4905e0f769167e1362f8c973b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623a32437525b92488112ad88f55f63d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
