    </node>
    <node id="布头">
      <data key="d0">布头</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">布头是布料剪裁后的剩余部分，也用于擦拭和清理机械设备。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89c33b1709aba69300fa32c8a1899f2e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="击卸">
      <data key="d0">击卸</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Impact removal is a simple method of disassembly that uses the force of a hammer to make the mating parts move relative to each other, achieving the disassembly purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="压卸和拉卸">
      <data key="d0">压卸和拉卸</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Pressing and pulling off are better than impact removal as they exert more uniform force, and the size and direction of the force can be controlled, reducing the possibility of part damage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="加热拆卸">
      <data key="d0">加热拆卸</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Heating disassembly uses the thermal expansion property of metal to disassemble parts, preventing parts from getting stuck or damaged during disassembly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="通用零部件的故障诊断与维修">
      <data key="d0">通用零部件的故障诊断与维修</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The fault diagnosis and maintenance of general parts involves various disassembly methods and maintenance procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of diagnosing and repairing general machine parts.&lt;SEP&gt;The text discusses the diagnosis and maintenance of general mechanical components, specifically focusing on gears.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-76f8d626c0daad789485fb4b40abae42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300b674808e0dab401bb885faad4bb34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="轴拆卸后的清洗、检查和修复">
      <data key="d0">轴拆卸后的清洗、检查和修复</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The cleaning, inspection, and repair of the shaft after disassembly are important steps in the maintenance process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="清洗">
      <data key="d0">清洗</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cleaning the disassembled mechanical parts is an important part of maintenance, involving removing oil, scale, carbon deposits, rust, and old coatings.&lt;SEP&gt;清洗是指在使用叶片泵前对管道进行彻底清洗，以去除污迹和氧化皮等。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35c2bb9ed0bc329c7dffda457d26e5a8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="主轴的检验">
      <data key="d0">主轴的检验</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The inspection of the main shaft involves checking for wear, surface damage, roundness error, straightness error, bending deformation, and other issues like keyway damage and thread damage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="形状和尺寸精度">
      <data key="d0">形状和尺寸精度</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Shape and size accuracy refers to the precise dimensions and form of parts, which are critical for proper assembly and function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="要求">
      <data key="d0">要求</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Requirements are specifications that parts must meet to ensure they fit and function correctly in an assembly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="配合">
      <data key="d0">配合</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Fit refers to how well parts are assembled together, which can be either interference fit or press fit.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of fitting the inner ring of a bearing to the shaft and the outer ring to the housing, affecting the bearing's radial clearance, running accuracy, and life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300b674808e0dab401bb885faad4bb34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="过盈配合">
      <data key="d0">过盈配合</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of fit where the bearing is pressed into the housing with a force greater than the clearance, suitable for heavy loads and high speeds.&lt;SEP&gt;Overfitting is a type of fit where parts are pressed together, requiring force to remove, often requiring specialized disassembly techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;The interference fit is a method of assembly where the part being inserted is slightly larger than the hole it fits into.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f4045e42394a6d45a6fa712b130bfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300b674808e0dab401bb885faad4bb34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="过渡配合">
      <data key="d0">过渡配合</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Transition fit is a type of fit that allows parts to be assembled with some play, easier to disassemble than overfitting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="击卸工具">
      <data key="d0">击卸工具</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Impact removal tools include hammers, mallets, punches, and blocks used to apply force to disassemble parts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="压床和拉模">
      <data key="d0">压床和拉模</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Press and pull dies are tools used for pressing and pulling off parts during disassembly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="拆卸处工作台">
      <data key="d0">拆卸处工作台</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The disassembly workbench is the surface where parts are removed from an assembly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="清洗液">
      <data key="d0">清洗液</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cleaning fluids are substances used to clean disassembled parts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="润滑脂">
      <data key="d0">润滑脂</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Lubricating grease is a substance used to prevent friction and wear between moving parts.&lt;SEP&gt;润滑脂是用于减少轴承摩擦和磨损的润滑材料。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faf021a1e9f43704271816ef558f91b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="木板或低平台">
      <data key="d0">木板或低平台</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Wooden boards or low platforms are used to store disassembled parts during maintenance or repair.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="专用箱子">
      <data key="d0">专用箱子</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Specialized boxes are used to store small disassembled parts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="长轴、丝杠等">
      <data key="d0">长轴、丝杠等</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Long shafts and screw threads are long, slender parts that require vertical suspension to prevent bending during storage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="误差相消法">
      <data key="d0">误差相消法</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Error cancellation method is a technique used to ensure the relative positions of parts are accurate during disassembly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="油">
      <data key="d0">油</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Oil is used to prevent rust and corrosion on disassembled parts during storage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="同轴度误差">
      <data key="d0">同轴度误差</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Axiality error refers to the degree of misalignment between the centerlines of different components.&lt;SEP&gt;Coaxiality error is the deviation from perfect alignment of the axis of a shaft with its housing.&lt;SEP&gt;The concentricity error is the deviation of the main shaft from being perfectly aligned with the axis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f4045e42394a6d45a6fa712b130bfe5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9faeed8bfe22cedda2f9a100d7b556bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0a9d9911a119de81d8e1c006a65b71</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752734</data>
