    <node id="安装">
      <data key="d0">安装</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of fitting a bearing onto a shaft or into a housing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-300b674808e0dab401bb885faad4bb34</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="轴承">
      <data key="d0">轴承</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The轴承, or bearings, are critical machine elements designed to support rotating parts in machinery and vehicles, while significantly reducing friction between moving surfaces. These components are integral to the proper operation of motors, as they constrain relative motion to the intended path and facilitate smooth rotation. Specifically, in the context of motors, bearings serve to support the shaft, thereby allowing it to rotate without excessive friction. They are essential for guiding the movement of parts and are integral to the functionality of the motor, as they not only support the shaft but also transmit motion. Issues with bearings, such as wear or uneven air gaps, can significantly impact the motor's performance, as noted in the case of uneven air gaps leading to operational issues. These components are thus fundamental in maintaining efficient and effective motor operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c0759493d2164571db1415c10cc5964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ba06ce22ee19f5d752b6523954299d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51df47410675f88b40ee5775ddf467a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e1e8bd51981f8100b6363185c3e9517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a115a0aab11c06dbf9d37ae8dc8807&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7717f9c647b8d45b1cefa44db848f23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faf021a1e9f43704271816ef558f91b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eba2a79b73acbc82d64797a0c6abe70</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752740</data>
    </node>
