    <node id="液压传动">
      <data key="d0">液压传动</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">液压传动是一种技术，其发展方向是高压、高速、大功率、高效、低噪声、低能耗、经久耐用、高度集成化。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752744</data>
    </node>
    <node id="液压泵">
      <data key="d0">液压泵</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The hydraulic pump is a critical mechanical device in hydraulic systems, responsible for generating pressure and flow. It operates by converting mechanical energy into hydraulic energy, thereby delivering hydraulic power to power machinery and equipment. This device is integral to the hydraulic transmission system, where it provides the necessary pressure energy to drive the system's working components. The hydraulic pump typically circulates fluid to achieve this, and its proper functioning is essential for the system to operate effectively.

Regular maintenance or replacement of the hydraulic pump is often required due to its exposure to continuous use and potential wear. It is designed to increase the pressure of a fluid within the hydraulic system, and its failure to do so, often due to the absence of oil or loose fittings, can result in the system experiencing low or no pressure.

Hydraulic pumps are built to provide both pressure and flow to the hydraulic system, with their performance significantly affecting system vibration and noise levels, as their mechanical energy conversion to fluid power can induce vibrations that influence the system's acoustics. As a core component of the hydraulic system, the hydraulic pump plays a pivotal role in ensuring that the system operates efficiently and reliably.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ba5e16308525584985e229da38004bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8a217882c9a1b2088793a95ff06b9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e927ef66eacdc3741d7a8dbda2d77531&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc8da9dbc945bf7a681df8813510d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce35f55aea19b816755795fdfbc6828b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96e2a482ca44d58c3fdc7888a608fdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07b41e601c2450e9357224ccdeaae5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9784ee50339b8dae5e16fe13763d736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cdee98ef526ceb57736fda4635f6616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcbbc0ef278995bc572c753ceef85338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906931c649f16a44721b0eebb71f69b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b267dc4b30d97dadf5f4201bc2406a7c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="过滤器">
      <data key="d0">过滤器</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The filter is a critical device designed to remove impurities and contaminants from fluids, including hydraulic oil in hydraulic systems and compressed air in pneumatic systems. As an integral component of both hydraulic and pneumatic systems, it serves to filter out particles that could otherwise cause damage or impair the system's performance. In the context of hydraulic systems, the filter is specifically engineered to filter and purify the hydraulic fluid, ensuring that it remains free of impurities that could lead to degradation or failure of the system. It is an auxiliary device that plays a vital role in maintaining the cleanliness and efficiency of hydraulic and pneumatic systems by preventing the entry of contaminants into the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3dc8da9dbc945bf7a681df8813510d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce35f55aea19b816755795fdfbc6828b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2347b9a7d0af4e8a8b655b61c5d5d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906931c649f16a44721b0eebb71f69b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcf0dd4905e0f769167e1362f8c973b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="溢流阀">
      <data key="d0">溢流阀</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The 溢流阀 is a crucial component in hydraulic systems, designed to control the flow of fluid or gas, primarily oil, to prevent overpressure. It functions as a pressure relief valve by allowing excess pressure to be released from the system when the pressure exceeds a predetermined threshold. This is achieved by enabling excess fluid to flow back to the reservoir or out of the system, thereby maintaining a stable and safe pressure level. The valve is instrumental in regulating and stabilizing the pressure within the hydraulic system, serving both as a control element and a safety device. When the overflow valve's orifice is blocked, it may lead to a lack of pressure in the system. In cases where the valve opens suddenly, it can cause the hydraulic pump to unload and lead to hydraulic shock. Overall, the 溢流阀 plays a pivotal role in preventing system damage and ensuring operational safety in hydraulic systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0f966e87923041bdf721a6c9dd71a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ba5e16308525584985e229da38004bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e3fd9231e91f4d605026c7e65ac9e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8a217882c9a1b2088793a95ff06b9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dba5683e0ed1465472acb33aeab7170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96e2a482ca44d58c3fdc7888a608fdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07b41e601c2450e9357224ccdeaae5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da66b4ba559873998867a86514a5f09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcbbc0ef278995bc572c753ceef85338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45c7f498930072d1430aac19bea884b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9e21580951e8a602128573cf01cefc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="节流阀">
      <data key="d0">节流阀</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The throttle valve, also known as a节流阀, is a category of flow control valves specifically designed for regulating the flow rate of fluid in hydraulic systems. This device is crucial in managing the flow of hydraulic fluid, and is often integral to the diagnosis and repair of hydraulic system issues. It functions by partially closing its orifice, thereby adjusting the flow rate of the fluid. As a control device, the throttle valve is utilized in a variety of systems, including engines, to regulate both pressure and flow rate. In hydraulic systems, it serves as a key component for controlling the flow and pressure of oil, ensuring optimal system performance. Essentially, the throttle valve is a type of valve used in hydraulic systems to manage fluid flow rate, characterized by its ability to modify the valve opening to achieve the desired flow control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9e3fd9231e91f4d605026c7e65ac9e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96e2a482ca44d58c3fdc7888a608fdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e23acdd91f6c00f8ea0955e56b43ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9e21580951e8a602128573cf01cefc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b90a52c6f070fb2b7a91103d66a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a60589f148604737e73dda0982c00b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c024958832b9f4d0025ff359e81b3839</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752756</data>
    </node>
    <node id="换向阀">
      <data key="d0">换向阀</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">The directional control valve, also known as 换向阀, is a crucial hydraulic component designed to alter the direction of fluid flow within a piping system. It plays a significant role in both system operations and maintenance, often being involved in identifying and repairing system issues. This hydraulic component is typically configured in a four-way or three-way arrangement to effectively manage the flow direction. It is instrumental in controlling the fluid direction, facilitating operations such as directional changes in hydraulic systems. Specifically, 换向阀 is utilized in hydraulic systems to change the oil pathways, which in turn enables the reciprocating movement of worktables or other machinery components. The device is also recognized for its role in managing fluid flow in a system, which is integral to its proper functioning and repair processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18214939792a5d3dcd493f164ba9b500&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96e2a482ca44d58c3fdc7888a608fdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07b41e601c2450e9357224ccdeaae5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0afc77668cb79a17228f50d78996acd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75a60589f148604737e73dda0982c00b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="电动机">
      <data key="d0">电动机</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The motor, a versatile electrical device, is primarily an electrical machine designed to convert electrical energy into mechanical energy. It serves as a pivotal power source in various applications, including hydraulic systems, gear pumps, and air compressors. The motor's operation is integral to mechanical operations and is used to drive systems such as guide rail 1 and guide rail 2 in piece pressing systems. It is a critical component in electrical control systems, often controlled by contactors.

Motor issues may arise, such as abnormal sounds and overheating, necessitating overcurrent protection and overloading prevention to avoid damage from excessive heat or electrical overload. Maintenance and operation of the motor are emphasized, with a focus on its various uses across industries, households, and commercial settings. The motor's conversion capabilities are highlighted, particularly its role as a source of power for hydraulic pumps, such as the gear pump, and its function within hydraulic systems, where its chambers are connected during operation.

The motor is also discussed in the context of potential failures, such as a fault in the thermal relay that could lead to overloading. Repair and maintenance scenarios are mentioned, indicating the importance of addressing the motor's different operational conditions. Overall, the motor is a robust and adaptable piece of equipment, central to a wide array of mechanical and industrial processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ccaecd9db63131912026a39494539cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e809e2424701c731a2da5e003621fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a115a0aab11c06dbf9d37ae8dc8807&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91db0f3b864a7198d442ec1ab788a5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa66717db2d8392ca7818f0ab87af2b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b267dc4b30d97dadf5f4201bc2406a7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7717f9c647b8d45b1cefa44db848f23a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcf0dd4905e0f769167e1362f8c973b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623a32437525b92488112ad88f55f63d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35c2bb9ed0bc329c7dffda457d26e5a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c5c0ac16b6c6ab477cbbbb517cca40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a14106bd728509626d998218e1f4815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af8795d4866f9a3fd7af5f9fcdd83b98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af5a36d856b334200291be646fe56c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0759493d2164571db1415c10cc5964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee9c850f2bcdf0f748d9c6a77d4b1f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e927ef66eacdc3741d7a8dbda2d77531&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faf021a1e9f43704271816ef558f91b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906931c649f16a44721b0eebb71f69b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="液压油">
      <data key="d0">液压油</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Hydraulic oil is a pivotal fluid in hydraulic systems, essential for the transmission of power, motion, and lubrication of components. It serves multiple functions within the system, including the prevention of overheating, the maintenance of system integrity, and the facilitation of smooth operation. As a critical medium in hydraulic systems, hydraulic oil must remain clean to prevent system failures and ensure the effective operation and maintenance of these systems. Its role is not only limited to transmitting energy but also includes lubricating system components, cooling the system, and providing密封功能 to maintain the system's efficiency and longevity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8a217882c9a1b2088793a95ff06b9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc8da9dbc945bf7a681df8813510d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96e2a482ca44d58c3fdc7888a608fdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4872ddd77cc800597c3ee787f9eb86f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2347b9a7d0af4e8a8b655b61c5d5d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9e21580951e8a602128573cf01cefc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b90a52c6f070fb2b7a91103d66a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25d02a948c6d8696d3214246a1d3817b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="液压系统故障">
      <data key="d0">液压系统故障</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">液压系统故障是液压传动系统在工作过程中可能出现的故障，原因包括设计、制造、使用不当和液压油污染等。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="设计原因">
      <data key="d0">设计原因</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">设计原因是导致液压系统故障的一个原因，指的是设计上的不合理性。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9e2c63145fc1bb1fe0be9ef3ce9a219</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="制造原因">
      <data key="d0">制造原因</data>
