      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="执行元件">
      <data key="d0">执行元件</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The actuating element, a critical component in hydraulic systems, serves as the part that performs the actual work within these systems. It encompasses devices such as cylinders or motors, which convert hydraulic energy into mechanical motion or force, thereby enabling the execution of tasks. These elements are subject to the influence of relief valves, which play a role in their performance. Maintenance and potential replacements may be necessary for actuating elements over time, as they are integral to the system's operation. The actuating element functions by transforming hydraulic energy into mechanical energy, and it is also considered an output component in the hydraulic system. Abnormal pressure in the actuator may indicate issues within the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ba5e16308525584985e229da38004bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc8da9dbc945bf7a681df8813510d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96e2a482ca44d58c3fdc7888a608fdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da66b4ba559873998867a86514a5f09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ef862a9e23d86099ddd8d1672a7b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e9e21580951e8a602128573cf01cefc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b90a52c6f070fb2b7a91103d66a84</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="振动和噪声">
