    <node id="传感器">
      <data key="d0">传感器</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The sensor is a device designed to detect physical input from its environment and convert it into an electrical signal, which is then utilized in control and monitoring systems. It is capable of experiencing various errors and interferences. This category encompasses a variety of sensor types, including Sensor 1, Sensor 3, and Sensor SE5V. Sensors play a crucial role in detecting and responding to stimuli such as temperature, pressure, or light. In the given example, a specific sensor is employed to detect the proximity of metal objects near the switch's terminal. Generally, sensors are used for the detection and measurement of physical quantities, ensuring accurate and reliable data collection in various applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-623a32437525b92488112ad88f55f63d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ba00d066e16d8a729e4d1d6be852341&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12b8d796408b133d3c0527a86eb30f6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5313a1b2bfcb93c2968ea3919437605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918985d61c599672b319aea8dbf10d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb01b0c8f343be722f1698f053da285</data>
