    <node id="电磁阀">
      <data key="d0">电磁阀</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The electromagnetic valve, also known as a solenoid valve, is a critical component in both pneumatic and hydraulic systems. It operates by utilizing an electric current to activate an electromagnet, which in turn controls the opening and closing of the valve. This mechanism is particularly effective in managing the flow of fluids, such as compressed air in pneumatic systems or hydraulic fluids in hydraulic systems. The solenoid valve functions by an electromagnetic coil, which acts as the primary control element. By activating the coil, the valve can be manipulated to either open or close, thereby regulating the flow of the fluid through the system. In hydraulic systems, the electromagnetic valve is specifically designed to control the flow of oil, ensuring precise and efficient operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-12b8d796408b133d3c0527a86eb30f6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce35f55aea19b816755795fdfbc6828b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5313a1b2bfcb93c2968ea3919437605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e23acdd91f6c00f8ea0955e56b43ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdcf0dd4905e0f769167e1362f8c973b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b267dc4b30d97dadf5f4201bc2406a7c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="活塞">
      <data key="d0">活塞</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The piston is a critical mechanical component found within hydraulic systems and engines, primarily responsible for reciprocating motion within a cylinder. It serves to generate force and movement, converting hydraulic energy into linear motion. This part is integral to both engines and hydraulic systems, where it often controls the flow of fluid or gas by opening or closing valves. The piston's movement is influenced by the pressure within the system, particularly in the buffer chamber. It may encounter issues such as stopping or rapid deceleration during the buffering process. The piston is also a part of a larger assembly that may experience complications, like piston seal wear, which can be addressed through appropriate maintenance and repair methods. In essence, the piston is a versatile and essential component in various applications that require the transformation of hydraulic energy into mechanical action.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7db0d804303b37c024cff2c6691c1842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46dfba00c0347934428630b20499263f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d81d1586fab16b83b27100e99262851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5313a1b2bfcb93c2968ea3919437605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67175ab18c23c1816a4f561e5a5d372b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51df47410675f88b40ee5775ddf467a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4872ddd77cc800597c3ee787f9eb86f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07b41e601c2450e9357224ccdeaae5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534fef71aa29d8e72825da70b7772d5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45c7f498930072d1430aac19bea884b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a4a03155fa2a96e34f47616ffe0cae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="活塞杆">
      <data key="d0">活塞杆</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The piston rod is a critical component within hydraulic cylinders that serves to connect the piston to the hydraulic system. It acts as a connecting rod, facilitating the transmission of force or motion between the piston and the cylinder. During operation, the piston rod can exhibit crawling motion, which may be influenced by factors such as poor assembly or the presence of small gaps that can lead to binding movement. As part of the hydraulic system, the piston rod is susceptible to damage or wear, and its primary function is to transfer linear motion from the piston to a connected mechanism. Specifically, it is the rod that connects the piston to the cylinder, ensuring the movement of the piston is effectively transmitted. The piston rod is also described as the part that links the piston to the cylinder cover, thereby contributing to the overall movement and functionality of the hydraulic cylinder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-205e5b50ed08e4587699576c3110fefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db0d804303b37c024cff2c6691c1842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12b8d796408b133d3c0527a86eb30f6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d81d1586fab16b83b27100e99262851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5313a1b2bfcb93c2968ea3919437605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67175ab18c23c1816a4f561e5a5d372b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51df47410675f88b40ee5775ddf467a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07b41e601c2450e9357224ccdeaae5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a4a03155fa2a96e34f47616ffe0cae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752786</data>
    </node>
