    <node id="电磁换向阀">
      <data key="d0">电磁换向阀</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The electromagnetic directional valve, known as 电磁换向阀, is a specialized type of valve designed to alter the direction of fluid or gas flow in hydraulic systems. This is achieved by utilizing an electromagnetic coil or electromagnet when an electrical signal is applied. The valve operates by applying electromagnetic force, which controls the fluid flow direction. It is a critical component in the control of fluid pathways, particularly in systems where quick direction changes are necessary. While the rapid switching capabilities of the 电磁换向阀 are advantageous, they may also generate hydraulic shock, which can affect system performance. This valve is specifically used to modify the flow direction in the control oil paths of hydraulic circuits leading to the two ends of a directional control valve, thereby playing a crucial role in the overall operation of electro-hydraulic directional control valves.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-763bd983c9440f6332b03769ffa52077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e23acdd91f6c00f8ea0955e56b43ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcbbc0ef278995bc572c753ceef85338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45c7f498930072d1430aac19bea884b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-537459fb97a3814b19b19a55238e2279&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19398f2e97c0d818beb2f7da07fc12c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
