    <node id="泄漏">
      <data key="d0">泄漏</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Leakage is a term that encompasses the escape of fluids, particularly hydraulic fluids, from a system or container. This phenomenon is often caused by valves that do not seal properly, resulting in fluid loss and potentially leading to system inefficiency. The occurrence of leakage can lead to various negative consequences such as damage to the system, reduced performance, increased temperatures, and overall degradation in the system's functionality. The description is consistent across the provided descriptions, with all highlighting the significance of proper sealing to prevent fluid loss and maintain optimal system performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e927ef66eacdc3741d7a8dbda2d77531&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce35f55aea19b816755795fdfbc6828b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763bd983c9440f6332b03769ffa52077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906931c649f16a44721b0eebb71f69b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cdee98ef526ceb57736fda4635f6616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25d02a948c6d8696d3214246a1d3817b</data>
