    <node id="密封件">
      <data key="d0">密封件</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The密封件, or seals, are essential mechanical devices designed to prevent the escape of fluid or gas from a system. These components are vital for maintaining tight seals, particularly in hydraulic systems where they are crucial for ensuring the integrity and functionality of the system. They serve as sealing elements that stop fluid leakage within hydraulic systems and are integral parts of valve assemblies where they prevent any potential leakage. Made from various materials, these sealing parts are used at joints in mechanical devices to avert fluid or gas leaks. Over time, seals may require replacement due to failure or damage, which can lead to the loss of buffering action when buffer chamber pressure is high. In summary,密封件 are integral components that play a critical role in maintaining the operational efficiency and safety of hydraulic systems by preventing leaks and maintaining system integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7db0d804303b37c024cff2c6691c1842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7f6ef4602a8cc5fe00045efd25f0fa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d81d1586fab16b83b27100e99262851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51df47410675f88b40ee5775ddf467a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4872ddd77cc800597c3ee787f9eb86f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da66b4ba559873998867a86514a5f09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07b41e601c2450e9357224ccdeaae5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b90a52c6f070fb2b7a91103d66a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52c6e3b4bdca7949382cf08a9307b76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
