    <node id="弹簧">
      <data key="d0">弹簧</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The spring is a versatile and essential component in various mechanical and hydraulic systems. It serves as a means to store potential energy and release it when required, thereby maintaining or changing the state of a system. Commonly utilized as an elastic element, the spring is designed to absorb energy and provide opposing force. In hydraulic systems, specific considerations are taken, such as ensuring the spring's hardness is appropriate and it is free from cracks or bends to maintain system integrity.

In the context of a hydraulic system, the spring functions as a critical component that may necessitate replacement or repair due to seal failure. It is integral to the valve assembly, where it exerts force to return the valve core to its original position. Additionally, the spring is a component within contactors, where it aids in providing pressure to facilitate the吸合 (attraction) and释放 (release) processes.

Within the realm of mechanical systems, the spring is a staple part, often found in devices such as the液控单向阀 (hydraulic check valve) and the直动式顺序阀 (direct-acting sequential valve). In these roles, the spring is responsible for delivering the necessary force to control the movement and positioning of the valve core, ensuring proper operation of the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7db0d804303b37c024cff2c6691c1842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c409a3cee64edbdc95bfdfc6401b9a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a14106bd728509626d998218e1f4815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e927ef66eacdc3741d7a8dbda2d77531&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da66b4ba559873998867a86514a5f09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ef862a9e23d86099ddd8d1672a7b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b90a52c6f070fb2b7a91103d66a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52c6e3b4bdca7949382cf08a9307b76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45c7f498930072d1430aac19bea884b8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
