    <node id="调压弹簧">
      <data key="d0">调压弹簧</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The 调压弹簧, also known as a pressure regulating spring, is a critical component designed to maintain a consistent pressure level within a system, particularly in pressure regulators. It serves to provide resistance and control the operation of hydraulic valves by adjusting the force exerted. This spring is adjustable, allowing for the modification of the pressure range in hydraulic systems. It is often used in conjunction with a regulating rod and is specifically tailored to regulate the pressure in hydraulic systems. The tension of the spring in a relief valve can be altered to change the pressure range, thereby ensuring optimal system performance and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3dba5683e0ed1465472acb33aeab7170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4872ddd77cc800597c3ee787f9eb86f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da66b4ba559873998867a86514a5f09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ef862a9e23d86099ddd8d1672a7b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52c6e3b4bdca7949382cf08a9307b76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45c7f498930072d1430aac19bea884b8</data>
