    <node id="PLC">
      <data key="d0">PLC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Programmable Logic Controller (PLC) is a crucial industrial digital computer that serves as the control core of various systems. It is designed to process signals from sensors and monitor input/output states to diagnose faults, thereby controlling the system's operations effectively. The PLC is instrumental in input/output port status detection and fault analysis, making it a pivotal component in electromechanical process automation. It stands for Programmable Logic Controller and is used to automate machinery and processes, ensuring the smooth operation of industrial systems. The device features input ports that can indicate signal status through LED indicators, enhancing the visibility of system status. Overall, the PLC is a versatile and essential tool in industrial automation, facilitating control and automation of various electromechanical systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-30e7e39b9a3610b864afa9c07a3004a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07931f37373e1b2ec4c7b188669c1e09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7020a9dc7fa252e8a0f9eab88fecb32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f385a3bd2ff1fdb44455a2c9c572dce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12b8d796408b133d3c0527a86eb30f6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce35f55aea19b816755795fdfbc6828b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918985d61c599672b319aea8dbf10d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd092a336c42ff6f15dddc88a96d87f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb01b0c8f343be722f1698f053da285&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f97d231de71b96f3f3b869aa0ce077f7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
