      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLC System">
      <data key="d0">PLC System</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">PLC System is a programmable logic controller system that is used for controlling industrial processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The PLC System is a control system that provides several diagnostic functions for the detection of faults and malfunctions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30e7e39b9a3610b864afa9c07a3004a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Strong Electric Interference">
      <data key="d0">Strong Electric Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Strong electric interference is a type of interference that affects the PLC system, often caused by dramatic changes in current or voltage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Control Cabinet Interference">
      <data key="d0">Control Cabinet Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Control cabinet interference occurs in control cabinets due to high-voltage electrical equipment, large inductive loads, and chaotic wiring, which can interfere with the PLC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Signal Line Interference">
      <data key="d0">Signal Line Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Signal line interference can be introduced through the power supply of transmitters or common signal instruments, as well as external induction interference on signal lines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grounding System Interference">
      <data key="d0">Grounding System Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Grounding system interference can occur when the grounding system is chaotic, potentially leading to large interference signals that affect the PLC system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal PLC System Interference">
      <data key="d0">Internal PLC System Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal PLC system interference is caused by the electromagnetic radiation between internal components and circuits of the PLC system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inverter Interference">
      <data key="d0">Inverter Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Inverter interference is caused by harmonics generated during the start-up and operation of inverters, which can lead to voltage distortion and affect the power quality of the grid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Power Supply">
      <data key="d0">Power Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Power supply is a crucial component in the PLC system, which is typically provided by a good-quality power supply to reduce interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cable Selection">
      <data key="d0">Cable Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Cable selection is an anti-interference measure where different types of signals are transmitted by different cables, and signal cables should be laid out separately according to the type of signal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hardware Filtering">
      <data key="d0">Hardware Filtering</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Hardware filtering involves connecting capacitors in parallel with the signal line and ground to reduce common mode interference, and adding filters to reduce differential mode interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software Anti-Interference Measures">
      <data key="d0">Software Anti-Interference Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Software anti-interference measures include digital filtering, frequency shaping sampling, correcting reference points, and information redundancy to improve software reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grounding Selection">
      <data key="d0">Grounding Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Grounding selection is an important anti-interference measure in the PLC system, which aims to ensure safety and suppress interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inverter Interference Suppression">
      <data key="d0">Inverter Interference Suppression</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Inverter interference suppression includes adding isolation transformers, using filters, and adding AC reactors to reduce electromagnetic radiation and interference to other equipment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electricity">
      <data key="d0">Electricity</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electricity is the energy source for the PLC System and is involved in the generation of electromagnetic interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electromagnetic Interference">
      <data key="d0">Electromagnetic Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Electromagnetic interference is a form of disturbance that affects the normal operation of the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Mode Interference">
      <data key="d0">Common Mode Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Common mode interference is a type of electromagnetic interference that occurs when two conductors are at the same potential with respect to a reference point.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Differential Mode Interference">
      <data key="d0">Differential Mode Interference</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Differential mode interference is a type of electromagnetic interference that occurs when two conductors are at different potentials with respect to a reference point.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grid">
      <data key="d0">Grid</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Grid is the electrical network that supplies power to the PLC System and is susceptible to electromagnetic interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Large Power Equipment">
      <data key="d0">Large Power Equipment</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Large Power Equipment refers to heavy-duty electrical devices that can generate significant electromagnetic interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonics">
      <data key="d0">Harmonics</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonics are unwanted frequencies that can be introduced into a power system by non-linear loads, affecting the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Short Circuit">
      <data key="d0">Short Circuit</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Short Circuit is an electrical fault that can cause a sudden increase in current, leading to electromagnetic interference in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transient Shock">
      <data key="d0">Transient Shock</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Transient shock refers to a sudden change in voltage or current that can affect the PLC System's operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transmitter">
      <data key="d0">Transmitter</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Transmitter is a device that sends signals to the PLC System, which can be a source of interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Instrument">
      <data key="d0">Instrument</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An Instrument is a device used to measure or monitor processes, which can also introduce interference to the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Grounding">
      <data key="d0">Grounding</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Grounding is the process of connecting an electrical system to the earth, which is used to reduce interference in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Signal Lines">
      <data key="d0">Signal Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Signal Lines are the conductors that carry data between components of the PLC System and can be sources of interference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Isolation Transformer">
      <data key="d0">Isolation Transformer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An Isolation Transformer is used to block electromagnetic interference from entering the PLC System.&lt;SEP&gt;An Isolation Transformer is used to isolate the PLC System from interference caused by the power supply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Filter">
      <data key="d0">Filter</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Filter is a device used to remove unwanted frequencies from a signal, which can help reduce interference in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Capacitor">
      <data key="d0">Capacitor</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Capacitor is an electronic component used to reduce common mode interference in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Filtering">
      <data key="d0">Digital Filtering</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital filtering is a software technique used to remove noise from a signal in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Frequency Shaping Sampling">
      <data key="d0">Frequency Shaping Sampling</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Frequency shaping sampling is a method used to improve the accuracy of measurements in the PLC System by shaping the frequency response of the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
