      <data key="d0">Reference Point电位校正</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Reference Point电位校正is a technique used to correct the potential of a reference point, which can help prevent potential drift in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dynamic Zero Point">
      <data key="d0">Dynamic Zero Point</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Dynamic Zero Point is a method used to maintain a stable reference point in the PLC System, preventing potential drift.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information Redundancy">
      <data key="d0">Information Redundancy</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Information redundancy is a technique used in software design to increase reliability and prevent errors in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1748752831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Software Flag Bits">
      <data key="d0">Software Flag Bits</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Software flag bits are used in software design to indicate the status of certain conditions in the PLC System.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1fa9f0ca2b19519536f8c80c3f2cbe87</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
